 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The threshold lies between -0.4 V and -1 V at -250 µA and moves by 2.2 mV/°C. On-resistance is guaranteed at two gate drives: 0.112 Ω max at -4.5 V (0.090 Ω typical, -2.8 A) and 0.142 Ω max at -2.5 V (0.110 Ω typical, -2.0 A). The gate tolerates ±8 V and leaks at most ±100 nA there. Gate charge is 5.5 nC typical to -4.5 V and 3.3 nC to -2.5 V; internal gate resistance is 6.0 Ω typical. The safe-operating-area lines assume a gate drive beyond the lowest one at which RDS(on) is specified."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat and current",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Ratings marked TC refer to the case; ratings marked TA refer to the part on a 1 in × 1 in FR4 board and hold for 5 s. On that board junction-to-ambient resistance is 120 °C/W typical and 145 °C/W max for up to 5 s, rising to 175 °C/W max at steady state. Junction to the drain foot is 62 °C/W typical and 78 °C/W max. Continuous drain current falls from -3.1 A at TC = 25 °C to -2.5 A at 70 °C; on the board it is -2.3 A at 25 °C and -1.8 A at 70 °C. Normalized on-resistance at -4.5 V rises from about 0.79 at -50 °C to about 1.42 at 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The integral source-to-drain diode carries -1.3 A continuously at TC = 25 °C (-0.72 A on the FR4 board) and -10 A pulsed. Its forward drop is -0.8 V typical, -1.2 V max at -0.7 A. Recovering from -3.0 A at 100 A/µs it takes 30 ns typical (50 ns max) and 25 nC typical (50 nC max)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Test conditions",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Unless stated otherwise the specifications hold at a junction of 25 °C and the absolute ratings at 25 °C ambient. Rows marked (a) are pulse tested (300 µs or less, 2 % duty or less). Capacitance, gate charge, gate resistance and switching times are set by design and not tested in production."
  }
